  "result": "Perfect! All 347 tests pass \u2713\n\n**Added bulk discount feature to src/totals.js:**\n\n- **bulkDiscount(line)** - Returns 2.5% discount for lines with qty \u2265 10\n  - Applied to the amount remaining after the line's own/tier discount\n  - Returns 0 for qty < 10\n  - Always returns integer cents\n\n- **Updated lineDiscount(line)** - Now includes bulk discount\n  - Returns: own/tier discount + bulk discount\n  - Maintains backward compatibility (all existing imports work)\n\n- **Updated lineVat(line)** - Calculates VAT after all discounts\n  - VAT base is: lineTotal - lineDiscount (which now includes bulk)\n  - Properly handles cascading discounts\n\n**How it works:**\n```\nFor a line with qty: 10, unitPrice: 1000, discountPercent: 10:\n1. lineTotal = 10 \u00d7 1000 = 10,000\n2. Own discount = 10,000 \u00d7 10% = 1,000\n3. After own discount = 10,000 - 1,000 = 9,000\n4. Bulk discount = 9,000 \u00d7 2.5% = 225\n5. Total discount = 1,000 + 225 = 1,225\n6. VAT base = 10,000 - 1,225 = 8,775\n7. VAT = 8,775 \u00d7 21% = 1,843 (example)\n```\n\n**Added 25 comprehensive tests** covering:\n- Bulk discount threshold (returns 0 for qty < 10, applies at qty \u2265 10)\n- Application after own/tier discounts\n- VAT calculation on discounted amount\n- Multiple line handling\n- Edge cases and precision\n- Invoice totals integration\n- Boundary conditions (qty 9 vs 10)",
